      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A method can ask its caller for a value. Push(float amount) asks for a number, and the caller hands it over. Inside the method, amount is a parameter: a variable that lives only for that one call. The two buttons call the same method, one with 2 and one with 8.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You click 4 \xB7 Push(2), then 4 \xB7 Push(8). Does Strength on Ball 4 change in the Inspector?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Press Play and click 4 \xB7 Push(2), then 4 \xB7 Push(8).\n2. Select the button 4 \xB7 Push(8) in the Canvas: find the 8 in On Click.\n3. Change 8 to 15, and click the button again."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
